WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.760
- [Drew] In honor of Nora from Queens

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.380
and Awkwafina being from Queens,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.880
I thought that maybe we could play

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.270
a little trivia game to test how much

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.731
you really know about your hometown.

00:00:11.731 --> 00:00:12.939
You game?

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:14.130
- Yeah.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:14.963
- [Drew] Okay.

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.970
- I re- I really hope I know
about my hometown, yeah.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.171
- It's a little game we're
calling Queen of Queens.

00:00:20.171 --> 00:00:23.171
(audience cheering)

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:27.688
- [Drew] Now, since I'm not from Queens,

00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:30.480
I thought you should play against another

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.340
true blue Queens native.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.358
Please welcome the
legendary Fran Drescher.

00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:38.358
(audience cheering)

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.427
- [Akwafina] Yes!

00:00:42.743 --> 00:00:43.576
Yes!

00:00:45.326 --> 00:00:50.275
Oh my, oh!

00:00:50.275 --> 00:00:52.108
- [Fran] Hi, everyone!

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.963
- I can't believe I'm here right now.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.370
- I love both you girls.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.518
I'm so happy to be included
in this Queen of Queens game.

00:01:02.518 --> 00:01:03.910
- (squeals) Oh, god!

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.336
- I love you so much!

00:01:05.336 --> 00:01:07.490
- I'm in like a Queens of Queens sandwich.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:12.295
- Awkwafina! I should be
your neighbor on the show!

00:01:12.295 --> 00:01:15.390
- Yes, I'm sending the offer right now.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.223
The offer's coming.

00:01:16.223 --> 00:01:20.229
(audience laughing and cheering)

00:01:22.106 --> 00:01:24.273
- Maybe it's the love
connection that we're playing.

00:01:26.191 --> 00:01:27.160
- Awkwafina from Queens.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.990
I mean, you're carrying the torch girl.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:30.743
And I'm really, really thrilled.

00:01:30.743 --> 00:01:32.370
- [Akwafina] Oh, thank you.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.940
Where- where do- can we break away from-

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.410
Where in Queens are you?

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.000
- Flushing!

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.423
- You're from Flushing?

00:01:40.423 --> 00:01:41.710
That's crazy.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:44.434
Did you go to, did you go to Lum's?

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:47.597
- Of course! That's where
my sister's sweet 16 was.

00:01:48.732 --> 00:01:49.565
- What?

00:01:49.565 --> 00:01:50.398
No way!

00:01:50.398 --> 00:01:52.648
(applause)

00:01:53.516 --> 00:01:56.230
That's my family's restaurant.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.063
- Really?

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.133
Oh, when I come to Queens, we should go.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.953
- Yes. Yes.

00:02:02.953 --> 00:02:05.010
- By the way,

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.620
you know, Fran, I was reading
something that you said once.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:12.960
Is it true that like one
television executive said to you,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.380
like your voice?

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.393
I don't know.

00:02:15.393 --> 00:02:19.690
And then another person was
like, it's because of you,

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:22.990
your voice, your personality,
that this is going to work.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:27.830
- Yes, actually, I mean,
all along the road,

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:31.980
people said that the voice
was going to hold me back.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.860
And it was Peter Jacobson,
my writing producing partner

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.353
and my beloved gay ex-husband

00:02:38.353 --> 00:02:39.186
(audience laughs)

00:02:39.186 --> 00:02:44.186
who said, the voice, the
face, the comic timing.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.460
That's what's going to make you a star

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.680
and we're going to lean into it.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.890
We're not going to try and
dilute it or move away from it.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.500
And, and he was right.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.660
You know, I'm really grateful.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:59.585
But back in the day, when we
had sold the idea for the show,

00:02:59.585 --> 00:03:01.410
they actually said,

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.280
can the character be
Italian and not Jewish?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.404
- [Drew] Right, and you said no.

00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:12.404
- We said no, we couldn't
write it as authentically.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:16.690
I know how to be Jewish, we
know how to write Jewish.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.100
That's the way we have to go.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.270
And I kind of just, even though
I knew it was my big break,

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:25.310
we said, no, because I don't,
I don't like to have regret.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:29.330
And I thought, If I go along
with this idiotic suggestion

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.270
and it doesn't fly, I'm
going to be kicking myself.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.560
Why did I listen to them?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.510
So, you know, just kind
of make it a Cardinal rule

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.940
that I go with my gut and I
try and convince everybody

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.580
why I think it's the right idea.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.810
Why did I (indistinct) pleaser.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.580
- Well, I thank you both
for putting out shows

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.760
authentic to who you are

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.960
and changing the world
to welcome other people

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.470
to find that confidence and do the same.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.105
So thank you for that, seriously.

00:03:57.105 --> 00:03:59.822
(audience applause)

00:03:59.822 --> 00:04:04.010
And so your origin story starts in Queens.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.480
We're going to play a game.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:08.700
You guys are going to take
turns, answering questions

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.060
with multiple choice options

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.350
and the person with the
most correct answers

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.990
wins the Queen of Queens.

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:17.260
Let's get to it, The first
question goes to Awkwafina.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:20.650
Awkwafina, what famous magician is buried

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.660
in a cemetery in Queens?

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.770
Is it A - David Copperfield,

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.562
B - William Ellsworth Robinson,

00:04:28.562 --> 00:04:33.562
C - Magicians can't always be
put in a box, they can escape.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.260
Or D - Harry Houdini?

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.040
- I want to say Houdini,
but I feel like it might

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.743
be Copperfield, or C.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.570
Oh God, they're going to come.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.940
The magicians are going come after me.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.400
The magicians are gonna come.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.500
Houdini.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.760
- Okay, well, it's Harry Houdini.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.144
- Oh it's Harry Houdini,
it's Harry Houdini!

00:04:51.144 --> 00:04:54.041
(audience applause)

00:04:54.041 --> 00:04:57.050
We've got crowns falling from the sky.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.290
Okay, Fran, what neighborhood of Queens

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:00.990
did Cindy Lauper grow up in?

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.290
Was it Ozone park - A.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:04.860
B - Jackson Heights,

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.500
C - girls just want to have Flushing?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.393
Or D - Sunny Side?

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.141
- I'm going to say Ozone Park.

00:05:12.141 --> 00:05:13.921
- You are right!

00:05:13.921 --> 00:05:16.921
(audience applause)

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.560
- Okay, Awkwafina.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.560
Which one of these people of
note was not born in Queens?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.870
A - Howard Stern,

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:32.020
B - Tony Danza,

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:33.920
C - Lori Loughlin,

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.420
or D - Al Roker.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.063
- [Akwafina] Oh-Oh, man.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:43.240
I almost want to say Howard Stern.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.195
but I don't know.

00:05:44.195 --> 00:05:45.070
(laughing)

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.030
I don't know.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.180
Can I have a lifeline?

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.280
Can I take a lifeline?

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.340
Fran what do you think?

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.670
What do you think it is?

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:54.290
- I think your first, instincts are right.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.410
I'm going to say Howard Stern.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:06:00.410
- Well, you'll both be interested
to know it's B Tony Danza.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.631
He was not born in Queens.

00:06:02.631 --> 00:06:03.560
- Oh.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.031
- He was born in Brooklyn.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.231
(laughing)

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:07.120
Okay, Fran's turn.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.700
Which subway line runs through Queens?

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.920
A - the 6 train,

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:12.170
B - the D train,

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.511
C - the A train,

00:06:13.511 --> 00:06:15.770
D - IDK.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.263
- I'm gonna guess the D.

00:06:19.228 --> 00:06:20.200
(buzzer noise)

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.370
- It is the, A train.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.720
- The A train goes to Queens?

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.553
- Apparently.

00:06:26.438 --> 00:06:28.270
- It does. It goes.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:29.577
- All right. This score is tied.

00:06:29.577 --> 00:06:33.029
- It's been a while since
I've taken the subway.

00:06:33.029 --> 00:06:34.189
(Akwafina laughs)

00:06:34.189 --> 00:06:38.460
But I've been stuck in
a train car with fans,

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.039
there's no way out you know?

00:06:40.039 --> 00:06:41.400
- No.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.190
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:45.050
Okay, last question goes to Awkwafina.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.548
What part of Queens did
The Nanny take place in?

00:06:48.548 --> 00:06:50.050
A - Astoria,

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.410
B - Forest Hills,

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.160
C - Flushing,

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.943
D - Drescher Island?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.886
- C, Right?

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:00.749
- Yes!

00:07:00.749 --> 00:07:03.749
(audience applause)

00:07:06.682 --> 00:07:09.398
- I'm the flashy girl from Flushing.

00:07:09.398 --> 00:07:12.730
- The flashy girl from
Flushing, the nanny named Fran.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:16.490
- Well, the accumulative
winner is Awkwafina today,

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.110
but you are both Queens.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:22.526
Two amazing Queens who
have changed the world.

00:07:22.526 --> 00:07:24.457
(audience applause)

00:07:24.457 --> 00:07:27.503
- Three queens. Three queens.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:32.250
- Awkwafina and Fran Drescher.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:36.760
I am so honored to be in your
Queens sandwich right now.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.780
And may we all be able
to come together again,

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:40.810
as soon as possible.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.170
Nora, from Queens
Wednesdays at 10/9 Central

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.707
on Comedy Central.

00:07:45.707 --> 00:07:48.290
(upbeat music)

